# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Private material: never tracked in this public repository.
#
# It lives in a separate private repository and appears here only as symbolic links. Every entry is written WITHOUT a
# trailing slash on purpose: a pattern ending in "/" matches directories only, and git sees a symlink to a directory as
# a link, not a directory, so "/docs/internal/" would NOT ignore the link. The slash form is listed as well so a real
# directory of the same name is ignored too. `git add -f` overrides all of this; bin/check-private-paths.sh (CI and the
# pre-commit hook) rejects such paths whatever .gitignore says.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Claude Code: project instructions, settings, commands, agents, skills, hooks, MCP servers, local memory
/CLAUDE.md
/CLAUDE.local.md
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md
.claude
.claude/
.mcp.json
.claudeignore

